# Normalize all text to LF in the repository AND on checkout, on every OS.
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites committed text
# files (.py/.json/.csv/.md/.tex) to CRLF on checkout, changing their bytes — which
# breaks every SHA-256 freeze manifest (week4/INTEGRATION, week5/RESULTS_FROZEN)
# with spurious "CHANGED" lines on a fresh clone. Pinning eol=lf keeps a clean clone
# byte-identical to the Linux blobs, so `--verify` passes on any platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artefacts: never apply line-ending conversion (it would corrupt them and,
# for the pinned .parquet/.png, also break the freeze hashes).
*.parquet binary
*.png binary
*.joblib binary
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
